.TH "SVGSCRIPTELEMENT.CROSSORIGIN" "3JS" "June 26, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGScriptElement.crossOrigin \- SVGScriptElement: crossOrigin property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]crossOrigin\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]SVGScriptElement\f[R] interface reflects the Cross\-Origin
Resource Sharing settings for the \f[CR]<script>\f[R] element.
For classic scripts from other origins, this controls whether full error
information will be exposed.
For module scripts, it controls the script itself and any scripts it
imports.
See CORS settings attributes for details.
.SH VALUE
A string containing a keyword specifying the CORS mode to use when
fetching the resource.
Possible values are:
.TP
\f[B]anonymous\f[R] or an empty string (\f[B]\(dq\(dq\f[R])
Requests sent by the \f[CR]SVGScriptElement\f[R] will use the
\f[CR]cors\f[R] \f[CR]Request.mode\f[R] and the \f[CR]same\-origin\f[R]
\f[CR]Request.credentials\f[R] mode.
This means that CORS is enabled and credentials are sent \f[I]if\f[R]
the resource is fetched from the same origin from which the document was
loaded.
.TP
\f[B]use\-credentials\f[R]
Requests sent by the \f[CR]SVGScriptElement\f[R] will use the
\f[CR]cors\f[R] \f[CR]Request.mode\f[R] and the \f[CR]include\f[R]
\f[CR]Request.credentials\f[R] mode.
All resources requested by the element will use CORS, regardless of
which domain the fetch is from.
.PP
If the \f[CR]crossOrigin\f[R] property is specified with any other
value, it is the same as specifying it as \f[CR]anonymous\f[R].
.PP
If the \f[CR]crossOrigin\f[R] property is not specified, the resource is
fetched without CORS (equivalent to using the \f[CR]no\-cors\f[R]
\f[CR]Request.mode\f[R] and the \f[CR]same\-origin\f[R]
\f[CR]Request.credentials\f[R] mode).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Accessing the \f[CR]crossOrigin\f[R] property
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R] xmlns=\(dqhttp://www.w3.org/2000/svg\(dq width=\(dq400\(dq height=\(dq200\(dq>
  <\f[B]script\f[R]
    id=\(dqmyScript\(dq
    href=\(dqhttps://example.com/script.js\(dq
    crossorigin=\(dqanonymous\(dq></\f[B]script\f[R]>
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] scriptElement = document.getElementById(\(dqmyScript\(dq);
console.log(scriptElement.crossOrigin); \f[I]// Output: \(dqanonymous\(dq\f[R]
.EE
